drm/amdgpu: let VCE suspend during a GPU reset while sessions are open

amdgpu_vce_suspend() returns -EINVAL when any encode session handle is
open. In a GPU reset that is the normal state: the hung encode job is
what triggered the reset. The error makes amdgpu_device_ip_suspend_phase2()
unwind at the very first block it tries (VCE is last in the VI block
list, so first in the reverse walk), leaving SMU, SDMA, GFX, GMC and IH
with status.hw set. amdgpu_device_pre_asic_reset() reports the error
but the ASIC reset goes ahead; afterwards every resume phase skips those
blocks because they still claim to be up, so nothing re-initialises
them and the SMU firmware is never reloaded. The GPU comes back dead:
"GPU reset succeeded, trying to resume" followed only by
"last message was failed ret is 0" every few seconds, on every reset
this Polaris10 machine has had (five of them, kernels 7.1.9 and 7.2.3).

During a reset the sessions cannot be preserved anyway -- the ASIC
reset drops them and VRAM is lost -- so clear the handles and let the
suspend succeed. UVD already suspends unconditionally.

Seen on an iMac18,3 (Radeon Pro 575, POLARIS10, DCE 11.2), triggered by
a VCE ring timeout under h264_vaapi encode.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vce.c	2026-09-11 13:50:59.311487670 +0300
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vce.c	2026-09-11 13:50:59.322594032 +0300
@@ -314,6 +314,24 @@
 	if (i == AMDGPU_MAX_VCE_HANDLES)
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * In a GPU reset the open sessions are already lost -- a hung encode
+	 * job is usually what triggered the reset, and the ASIC reset drops
+	 * every session regardless. Refusing to suspend here makes
+	 * amdgpu_device_ip_suspend_phase2() unwind before it reaches the
+	 * blocks behind VCE (SMU, SDMA, GFX, GMC, IH), so after the reset
+	 * they still report hw=true, are never re-initialised, and the GPU
+	 * comes back without SMU firmware. Drop the handles and let the
+	 * suspend go through.
+	 */
+	if (amdgpu_in_reset(adev)) {
+		for (i = 0; i < AMDGPU_MAX_VCE_HANDLES; ++i) {
+			atomic_set(&adev->vce.handles[i], 0);
+			adev->vce.filp[i] = NULL;
+		}
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/* TODO: suspending running encoding sessions isn't supported */
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
